       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 200 mg/day. Doses that high raise the risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures, and GI or bleeding effects. Your patient's normal renal and hepatic function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n\n1. **A typo or a different dose.** Common doses are 50 mg, 100 mg, or 200 mg once daily. Starting doses are usually 25\u201350 mg.\n2. **A deliberate dose above the maximum.** If so, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that it's intentional, for example \"Dose exceeds labeled max; attending-confirmed.\" Please also tell me about any interacting drugs, such as other serotonergic agents or QT-prolonging drugs, and whether you want an ECG or other monitoring.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
